<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Diamond samples encouraging - Kimberley.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Diamond samples encouraging - Kimberley.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kimberley Diamond Co NL said on Tuesday it was encouraged by the recovery of 12 diamonds weighing a total 5.35 carats from a bulk sampling programme at its Blina property in Western Australia.</p>
<p>The average diamond size was 0.45 carats and the largest stone weighed 2.31 carats, the company said.</p>
<p>Kimberley said it is working on a programme of drilling and shallow pitting to define the immediate extent of gravels around its number five pit. More extensive bulk sampling is also planned to determine grade continuity and to confirm diamond quality, it said.    -- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
